\n            </summary>\r\n            <div class=\"bench-card-detail\">\r\n              \r\n              <p style=\"margin:0\"><b>Procedure:</b>\r\n                Check the recirculation-line mid-point quick-connect for a loose connection.</p>\r\n              \r\n                <p class=\"small muted\" style=\"margin:0\">Tool: Hands. Two minutes.</p>\r\n              \r\n              <p class=\"bench-pass-line\" style=\"margin:0\">Pass = Connector fully seated and latched.</p>\r\n              \r\n                <p class=\"small muted\" style=\"margin:0\">If abnormal: Reseat it; this is FCA&#39;s documented first check for exactly these codes. Re-verify (below) before doing anything else.</p>\r\n              \r\n              \r\n                <p class=\"small\" style=\"margin:0\">Doc:\r\n                  <a href=\"#tsb-S2125000002\">S2125000002</a>\r\n                   &mdash; EVAP leak codes -- check the recirculation-line quick-connect first</p>\r\n              \r\n              \r\n                <ul class=\"bench-inspect-steps small muted\">\r\n                  \r\n                    <li>purge_valve_connector: hose routing and connector seating at the ejector tees (visual + wiggle test) &mdash; TSB 9100325 Rev 1</li>\r\n                  \r\n                    <li>esim_connector: connector corrosion/seating; housing wet with fuel (visual) &mdash; TSB 9100471</li>\r\n                  \r\n                    <li>esim_ground: ground integrity (voltage-drop test) &mdash; none -- TechAuthority</li>\r\n                  \r\n                </ul>\r\n              \r\n\r\n              <form method=\"post\" action=\"/v/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/bench/done\" id=\"form-evap-1\" class=\"bench-outcome-fields\">\r\n                <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"step_id\" value=\"evap-1\">\r\n                <select name=\"outcome\">\r\n                  <option value=\"ok\" >OK</option>\r\n                  <option value=\"fault_found\" >Fault found</option>\r\n 